# Known equivalent changes, kept out on purpose (each guard is also made by something else, so removing it alone changes nothing a caller can see):
#   * the `user_id is not null and org_id is null` shape in team_require_owner / team_list: a business profile either has a user or an org, never both nor neither (the table's own
#     shape check), so dropping one half still turns away the venues and event groups;
#   * `e.org_id is not null` / `e.org_id is null` in the event checks: is_org_member(null, ...) is false, so an event with no business is turned away either way;
#   * `e.venue_id <> v_venue` without the null tests: a comparison with null is not true, so an event with no venue yet is still allowed;
#   * `profile_can_act_as` in hire_side: every function that asks for the side has just called profile_require_actor / profile_require_permission, which say the same;
#   * the `awaiting_deposit`-only branch of the pending list for an agreed hire: professionals can be attached only once the hire is confirmed.
